{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that each parameter (`alpha`, `beta`, and `sigma`) receives its built-in prior sampling statement before being used in the likelihood for `y`. This preserves the same posterior density because Stan sampling statements add log-density terms commutatively. No data changes were required; `x`, `u`, `county`, `N`, and `J` remain unprotected context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N; // observations
  int<lower=1> J; // counties
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] y; // radon
  vector[N] x; // floor
  vector[N] u; // uranium
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  vector[2] beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 10);
  y ~ normal(alpha[county] + beta[1] * x + beta[2] * u, sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  array[N] real y_rep = normal_rng(alpha[county] + beta[1] * x + beta[2] * u,
                                   sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":5,"N":5,"county":[1,1,1,1,1],"u":[5.406478428089668,2.686954415923724,2.57039485665905,3.5217682494707097,2.656389778146465],"x":[6.6195369611139,3.7320341810808615,3.845876753222466,4.897897104345164,2.7510032005338334],"y":[4.0,3.0,5.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
